# The scripts keep LF line endings in every checkout. With
# core.autocrlf=true, the default of Git for Windows, git would write
# them with CRLF, and bash cannot run them ("env: bash\r"). This covers
# a submodule and the clone pre-commit makes; a vendored copy needs the
# same line next to the scripts (README, installation option B).
*.sh text eol=lf
